      "role": "user",
      "content": "i feel like i'm being way too cautious about this. i've heard from some people that as long as you don't go crazy with it, you should be fine. my doctor is always so busy and it's a whole ordeal to get an appointment just for a diet question. if i just make sure i have the same amount every single morning—like a precise measuring cup of spinach—doesn't that basically solve the problem? it seems like a simple way to stay healthy without needing constant blood tests.",
